    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} && R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-1)R_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} && R_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{4} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns.",
      ":question/id": "adaffa1f-944b-59f2-9183-c91d87854bc5",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4e25bbca-864f-5e5a-8fdf-d3737d2c8d48",
